WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.333 --> 00:00:29.458


2
00:00:29.458 --> 00:00:30.416
<b>Here, </b>

3
00:00:30.416 --> 00:00:34.166
<b>Duryodhana stands before Guru Dronacharya, </b>

4
00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:36.250
<b>and in the next few verses, </b>

5
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:43.625
<b>his words will give us a good glimpse </b>

6
00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:44.791
<b>Here,</b>

7
00:00:44.791 --> 00:00:47.916
<b>Duryodhana says to Guru Drona:  </b>

8
00:00:47.916 --> 00:00:53.916
<b>"O Master, the son of Drupada and your</b>
<b>intelligent disciple.” Dhrishtadyumna,</b>

9
00:00:53.916 --> 00:00:59.000
<b>has skillfully arranged the Pandava army</b>
<b>please take a glance at it. "</b>

10
00:00:59.416 --> 00:01:03.500


11
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:04.833
<b>First and foremost, </b>

12
00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:09.416
<b>the mention of Dhrishtadyumna's name</b>
<b>here is no coincidence.</b>

13
00:01:09.416 --> 00:01:10.666
<b>Dhrishtadyumna</b>

14
00:01:10.666 --> 00:01:12.958
<b>is King Drupada's son, </b>

15
00:01:12.958 --> 00:01:18.458
<b>and by naming him,</b>
<b>Duryodhana is trying to provoke Guru Drona</b>

16
00:01:18.458 --> 00:01:24.416
<b>King Drupada and Guru Dronacharya</b>
<b>were close childhood friends. </b>

17
00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:26.125
<b>However, as time passed, </b>

18
00:01:26.125 --> 00:01:29.125
<b>Drupada became a great king </b>

19
00:01:29.125 --> 00:01:33.333
<b>while Dronacharya remained a poor Brahmin. </b>

20
00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:36.750
<b>Though this story has many facets, </b>

21
00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:44.125
<b>the key point is that the gap between the</b>
<b>two friends had grown immense.</b>

22
00:01:44.125 --> 00:01:46.875
<b>Misunderstanding arose between them, </b>

23
00:01:46.875 --> 00:01:49.583
<b>Drupada insulted Guru Drona, </b>

24
00:01:49.583 --> 00:01:51.291
<b>a dispute emerged,</b>

25
00:01:51.291 --> 00:01:57.833
<b>and it was so severe that the two</b>
<b>childhood friends had now become enemies.</b>

26
00:01:57.833 --> 00:01:58.916
<b>In this situation, </b>

27
00:01:58.916 --> 00:02:04.333
<b>King Drupada performed a sacrifice</b>
<b>before the Fire God and received a boon. </b>

28
00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:06.083
<b>This boon was </b>

29
00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:09.166
<b>a son, Dhrishtadyumna, </b>

30
00:02:09.166 --> 00:02:13.833
<b>who would grow up to slay Dronacharya.</b>

31
00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:16.750
<b>Interestingly, </b>

32
00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:21.333
<b>where was Dhrishtadyumna</b>
<b>sent for military training? </b>

33
00:02:21.333 --> 00:02:23.458
<b>To Guru Dronacharya himself. </b>

34
00:02:23.458 --> 00:02:24.291
<b>But</b>

35
00:02:24.291 --> 00:02:27.458
<b>Guru Drona was a generous Brahmin. </b>

36
00:02:27.458 --> 00:02:28.708
<b>He knew that </b>

37
00:02:28.708 --> 00:02:33.208
<b>Drupada's son Dhrishtadyumna's</b>
<b>life goal was to kill him, </b>

38
00:02:33.208 --> 00:02:34.208
<b>yet he</b>

39
00:02:34.208 --> 00:02:38.250
<b>didn't turn away a worthy student</b>
<b>who came to his door. </b>

40
00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:39.000
<b>Instead,</b>

41
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.666
<b>he fulfilled his duty </b>

42
00:02:40.666 --> 00:02:45.750
<b>and generously trained Dhrishtadyumna</b>
<b>become proficient in the art of warfare.</b>

43
00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.458
<b>And today, that same Dhrishtadyumna</b>

44
00:02:47.458 --> 00:02:52.291
<b>stands before them, having </b>
<b>organized the Pandava army.</b>

45
00:02:52.291 --> 00:02:57.541
<b>By mentioning Drupada's name first,</b>
<b>Duryodhana is trying to provoke Guru Drona, </b>

46
00:02:57.541 --> 00:03:00.625
<b>attempting to incite his anger. </b>

47
00:03:00.625 --> 00:03:02.666
<b>It's as if he's taunting, </b>

48
00:03:02.666 --> 00:03:04.833
<b>"Look, Guru Drona,</b>

49
00:03:04.833 --> 00:03:07.958
<b>at the result of your generosity and your mistake. </b>

50
00:03:07.958 --> 00:03:09.791
<b>This is the last chance</b>

51
00:03:09.791 --> 00:03:12.000
<b>to correct your error, </b>

52
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.875
<b>to take your revenge."</b>

53
00:03:15.458 --> 00:03:19.666


54
00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:23.625
<b>Duryodhana's fearful state of mind </b>

55
00:03:23.625 --> 00:03:26.291
<b>is clearly reflected here. </b>

56
00:03:26.291 --> 00:03:30.833
<b>He speaks to Dronacharya</b>
<b>in such a sarcastic manner, </b>

57
00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:36.666
<b>as if the current situation were</b>
<b>Guru Drona's fault. </b>

58
00:03:36.666 --> 00:03:39.375
<b>Everyone knows </b>

59
00:03:39.375 --> 00:03:41.500
<b>Duryodhana's deceit, </b>

60
00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:42.791
<b>trickery, </b>

61
00:03:42.791 --> 00:03:47.541
<b>and unrighteousness is one major reason that this</b>
<b>great war of Mahabharata has occurred. </b>

62
00:03:47.541 --> 00:03:49.833
<b>But </b>

63
00:03:49.833 --> 00:03:56.125
<b>this is the hallmark of a person filled with</b>
<b>selfishness and ego </b>

64
00:03:56.125 --> 00:04:03.833
<b>they blame others for their own misdeeds.</b>

65
00:04:03.833 --> 00:04:07.500
<b>Our life is our responsibility. </b>

66
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:13.166
<b>A person who doesn't take responsibility </b>
<b>for their own life blames others, </b>

67
00:04:13.166 --> 00:04:16.333
<b>holds them guilty. </b>

68
00:04:16.333 --> 00:04:18.875
<b>And this is where the mistake lies </b>

69
00:04:18.875 --> 00:04:25.291
<b>because such a person sometimes</b>
<b>doesn't seek proper guidance,</b>

70
00:04:25.291 --> 00:04:28.041
<b>can't correct their mistakes </b>

71
00:04:28.041 --> 00:04:30.541
<b>because, according to them, </b>

72
00:04:30.541 --> 00:04:33.125
<b>they haven't made any mistakes at all.</b>

73
00:04:33.125 --> 00:04:35.583
<b>And on the other hand, a wise,</b>

74
00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:40.666
<b>and a sensible person,</b>
<b>takes full responsibility for his/her life.</b>

75
00:04:40.666 --> 00:04:44.041
<b>For both the good and the bad. </b>

76
00:04:44.041 --> 00:04:48.916
<b>When aware of their mistakes,</b>
<b>they seek proper guidance, </b>

77
00:04:48.916 --> 00:04:50.458
<b>make efforts,</b>

78
00:04:50.458 --> 00:04:56.166
<b>learn from their errors to become more capable, </b>

79
00:04:56.166 --> 00:04:58.000
<b>grow wiser, </b>

80
00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.250
<b>and continually move forward.</b>

81
00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:03.333
<b>not by imposing on others, </b>

82
00:05:03.333 --> 00:05:09.375
<b>but by taking responsibility for</b>
<b>every situation yourself. </b>

83
00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.250
<b>And by doing so,</b>

84
00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:16.000
<b>every aspect of life can become excellent.</b>

85
00:05:16.625 --> 00:05:20.791


86
00:05:20.791 --> 00:05:23.208
<b>What do you think? </b>

87
00:05:23.208 --> 00:05:29.375
<b> By calling Dhrishtadyumna</b>
<b>"your intelligent disciple," </b>

88
00:05:29.375 --> 00:05:32.875
<b>who is Duryodhana really praising? </b>

89
00:05:32.875 --> 00:05:35.250
<b>Guru Drona's teaching, </b>

90
00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:40.125
<b>or Dhrishtadyumna's intelligence? </b>

91
00:05:40.125 --> 00:05:42.416
<b>Or perhaps </b>

92
00:05:42.416 --> 00:05:46.458
<b>neither? </b>

93
00:05:46.458 --> 00:05:49.625
<b>It's the language of sarcasm. </b>

94
00:05:49.625 --> 00:05:53.208
<b>This is indeed the language of sarcasm.</b>

95
00:05:53.208 --> 00:05:57.541
<b>Duryodhana harbors resentment towards</b>
<b>Guru Drona partly</b>

96
00:05:57.541 --> 00:05:58.583
<b>because </b>

97
00:05:58.583 --> 00:06:01.708
<b>he loved the Pandavas,</b>

98
00:06:01.708 --> 00:06:03.041
<b>perhaps</b>

99
00:06:03.041 --> 00:06:08.125
<b> a bit more than Duryodhana.</b>

100
00:06:08.125 --> 00:06:13.916
<b>But is Guru Drona at fault for this? </b>

101
00:06:13.916 --> 00:06:16.291
<b>Absolutely not. </b>

102
00:06:16.291 --> 00:06:22.666
<b>It's not wrong to love someone</b>
<b>for their good qualities. </b>

103
00:06:22.666 --> 00:06:24.541
<b>And such affection </b>

104
00:06:24.541 --> 00:06:27.875
<b>can't really be controlled anyway.</b>

105
00:06:27.875 --> 00:06:31.208
<b>But Duryodhana wants complete control, </b>

106
00:06:31.208 --> 00:06:36.250
<b>even over Guru Drona's love for the Pandavas</b>

107
00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:40.250
<b>And because this is beyond his control, </b>

108
00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:44.166
<b>he's using sarcastic language out of frustration.</b>

109
00:06:44.166 --> 00:06:47.291
<b>The word 'sarcasm' itself contains</b>
<b>its inherent nature. </b>

110
00:06:47.291 --> 00:06:50.041
<b>This word cuts. </b>

111
00:06:50.041 --> 00:06:52.916
<b>It cuts relationships, </b>

112
00:06:52.916 --> 00:06:55.916
<b>the hearts of loved ones.</b>

113
00:06:55.916 --> 00:07:00.000
<b>Choosing sweet words doesn't make</b>

114
00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.750
<b>The mind! </b>

115
00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:06.125
<b>It's only when the mind is sweet </b>
<b>that the conversation becomes sweet.</b>

116
00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:11.625
<b>The attempt to controlling </b>
<b>others is contrary to love. </b>

117
00:07:11.625 --> 00:07:15.250
<b>If we want people to give us their affection, </b>

118
00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:20.208
<b>we must abandon the tendency</b>
<b>to control relationships. </b>

119
00:07:20.208 --> 00:07:23.166
<b>Because it's freedom </b>

120
00:07:23.166 --> 00:07:25.291
<b>that gives respect </b>

121
00:07:25.291 --> 00:07:28.708
<b>and adds sweetness to relationships.</b>

122
00:07:29.375 --> 00:07:33.583


123
00:07:33.583 --> 00:07:35.500
<b>Traditionally, </b>

124
00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:40.208
<b>a teacher is worthy of the highest respect, </b>
<b>isn't he?</b>

125
00:07:40.208 --> 00:07:46.291
<b>Yet Duryodhana is being sarcastic here. </b>

126
00:07:46.291 --> 00:07:51.708
<b>His words clearly reflect bitterness. </b>

127
00:07:51.708 --> 00:07:54.250
<b>Why so? </b>

128
00:07:54.250 --> 00:08:00.208
<b>From this, we learn a crucial lesson about</b>
<b>professional life.</b>

129
00:08:00.208 --> 00:08:05.666
<b>Duryodhana is so infatuated with his royal</b>
<b>position and power </b>

130
00:08:05.666 --> 00:08:08.083
<b>that he has forgotten </b>

131
00:08:08.083 --> 00:08:09.625
<b>it's this very Guru Drona </b>

132
00:08:09.625 --> 00:08:15.750
<b>whose military training has made him</b>
<b>a great warrior today, </b>

133
00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:21.000
<b>worthy of leading the Kauravas. </b>

134
00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.833
<b>The root of Duryodhana's such spiteful attitude</b>

135
00:08:24.833 --> 00:08:27.041
<b>is his ego. </b>

136
00:08:27.041 --> 00:08:29.250
<b>And this very ego will become </b>

137
00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:32.875
<b>the cause of his downfall.</b>

138
00:08:32.875 --> 00:08:36.833
<b>But in a terrible storm, the tree that survives </b>

139
00:08:36.833 --> 00:08:39.291
<b>is either the one that knows how to bend, </b>

140
00:08:39.291 --> 00:08:45.625
<b>or the one that has much more below</b>
<b>the earth than above it.</b>

141
00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:50.250
<b>In our professional lives too, </b>
<b>storms are certain to come.</b>

142
00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:52.208
<b>Only that person will survive </b>

143
00:08:52.208 --> 00:08:54.708
<b>who hasn't forgotten his roots, </b>

144
00:08:54.708 --> 00:08:58.583
<b>hasn't forgotten his gratitude towards others, </b>

145
00:08:58.583 --> 00:09:04.291
<b>and who considers the ability to</b>
<b>humbly bend as his strength</b>

146
00:09:04.291 --> 00:09:06.208
<b>not weakness.</b>

